# Sharing pytest fixtures

## Description

When people start using pytest as a team, they often come up with cool fixtures that would be great to share across projects. Many great Python packages, including Faker, come pre-loaded with pytest fixtures. This talk describes how easy it is to share fixtures using the pytest plugin model. The talk follows the journey of a pytest fixture from local fixture to pip installable pytest plugin using modern Python packaging.  

## Outline

* Fixture crash course (5 min)
    * What are fixtures
    * Walking through a couple examples 
    * Using them in test code
* Sharing fixtures within a project (5 min)
    * Sharing with conftest.py files
* Sharing between projects (building a plugin) (15 min)
    * Moving fixtures into their own Python project
    * Packaging with flit
    * What needs to be in pyproject.toml
    * Specifying pytest entry points
    * Alternative settings for hatch & setuptools
* Sharing through github repo (1 min)
* Testing plugins with tox (3 min)
* Sharing through PyPI (1 min)

